WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.015
Welcome to the Pipeline Fortress capstone
presentation Pipeline Fortress

00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:08.522
integrates security checks into software
delivery for the OWASP Juice

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:13.007
Shop training application The recorded work
covers six security stages

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:16.334
and reduces the eleven baseline critical
issues to zero in retained

00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:20.400
source and image scans The selected
application evidence records two

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.886
thousand three hundred and thirty two
passing tests The published

00:00:23.896 --> 00:00:27.372
version one point zero point zero release
includes all three focused

00:00:27.382 --> 00:00:28.861
infrastructure remediations

00:00:30.736 --> 00:00:34.322
This walkthrough explains how the pipeline
links each security decision

00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:38.808
to a specific source revision and image We
will examine the implementation

00:00:38.948 --> 00:00:43.303
the measured results and the controls
around AI assisted triage The

00:00:43.313 --> 00:00:46.840
presentation uses recorded project evidence
and a synthetic narrator

00:00:47.529 --> 00:00:50.965
Detailed receipts and reproduction
instructions accompany the submission

00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:55.767
The project team and presenters are

00:00:57.176 --> 00:00:58.055
Gunda Swetha

00:00:59.672 --> 00:01:00.941
Sudheer Kumar Thammana

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.539
Sravani Avadurthi

00:01:04.952 --> 00:01:05.731
Nikhil Kumar

00:01:07.448 --> 00:01:08.167
Amit Saini

00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:13.700
The next slides explain the engineering
objective the pipeline architecture

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:18.225
and the verification behind the release We
then examine security coverage

00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:21.792
the AI data boundary and the measured
limits of the evaluation

00:01:23.655 --> 00:01:27.681
The source code report and evidence files
support the technical discussion

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.686
Each reported result retains its own
execution scope The team credits

00:01:32.696 --> 00:01:36.012
identify the presenters without assigning
individual implementation

00:01:36.022 --> 00:01:40.108
roles that the evidence does not establish
Let us begin with the delivery

00:01:40.118 --> 00:01:41.706
problem that the project addresses

00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:48.062
The brief describes an engineering team
that releases frequently and

00:01:48.072 --> 00:01:52.258
receives security feedback too late
Pipeline Fortress moves selected

00:01:52.268 --> 00:01:55.764
checks into the build and review process so
developers can see findings

00:01:55.774 --> 00:01:59.800
before a release decision The target is a
pinned Juice Shop application

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:04.166
in an owned training environment No
external systems or customer data

00:02:04.176 --> 00:02:04.845
are included

00:02:06.704 --> 00:02:11.130
The implementation includes static analysis
dependency analysis secrets

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:14.746
scanning infrastructure checks container
scanning and passive web

00:02:14.756 --> 00:02:18.642
scanning The submission documents the
implemented controls and their

00:02:18.652 --> 00:02:22.608
verification evidence The scenario mentions
catching eighty percent

00:02:22.618 --> 00:02:26.614
of vulnerabilities before merge The
available evaluation measures

00:02:26.624 --> 00:02:30.659
a small labeled fixture set It cannot
establish an eighty percent

00:02:30.669 --> 00:02:34.056
detection rate across the whole application
or a production service

00:02:36.953 --> 00:02:39.790
The workflow starts with a pinned source
checkout and the selected

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.825
application build and test sequence Source
scanners inspect code dependencies

00:02:44.955 --> 00:02:48.931
history and the working tree A separate
build produces the hardened

00:02:48.941 --> 00:02:53.436
image Container analysis and software
inventory operate on that exact

00:02:53.446 --> 00:02:56.903
image and the staging job deploys the
transferred artifact into an

00:02:56.913 --> 00:03:01.178
owned temporary Kubernetes cluster Passive
web scanning follows functional

00:03:01.188 --> 00:03:02.057
runtime checks

00:03:03.923 --> 00:03:07.829
Each job publishes a sanitized receipt with
its run revision source

00:03:07.839 --> 00:03:12.604
identity and relevant hashes The aggregate
job checks those identities

00:03:12.614 --> 00:03:16.670
before accepting the execution This
prevents a passing report from

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.736
one revision being combined with an
unrelated build or deployment

00:03:20.436 --> 00:03:23.642
The workflow uses pinned action revisions
and read only repository

00:03:23.652 --> 00:03:27.728
permissions Cleanup removes the temporary
staging resources belonging

00:03:27.738 --> 00:03:28.388
to that run

00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:34.591
The release on main completes all eight
workflow jobs successfully

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:38.298
at the recorded release revision The
retained application evidence

00:03:38.308 --> 00:03:41.344
contains two thousand three hundred and
thirty two passing tests and

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:45.740
six skips Nine tests that depend on
external service availability

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:50.115
are excluded from the offline profile
Server verification goes beyond

00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:54.091
a summary count All four hundred and twenty
four expected case and

00:03:54.101 --> 00:03:58.037
status identities match across forty one
files including five critical

00:03:58.047 --> 00:03:58.986
regression cases

00:04:00.853 --> 00:04:04.150
This matters because an earlier run omitted
eleven server verdicts

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.306
and the gate correctly rejected it The
accepted historical publication

00:04:08.316 --> 00:04:12.631
recorded eighty five safeguard contracts
Release preparation expanded

00:04:12.641 --> 00:04:16.018
verification to one hundred and twenty five
local contracts including

00:04:16.028 --> 00:04:20.084
the source gate checks These counts
describe distinct verification

00:04:20.094 --> 00:04:24.219
scopes The release evidence and earlier
scanner snapshots retain their

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:25.988
own revision and execution dates

00:04:28.897 --> 00:04:32.903
Each scanner addresses a different part of
the delivery path Semgrep

00:04:32.913 --> 00:04:37.028
applies authored source rules Trivy
examines dependency and image

00:04:37.038 --> 00:04:40.885
inventories Gitleaks checks both Git
history and the current tree

00:04:41.584 --> 00:04:45.290
Checkov evaluates infrastructure and Docker
configuration while ZAP

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.807
performs a passive scan of the deployed
application

00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:53.966
A completed scanner is not the same as a
clean security result The

00:04:53.976 --> 00:04:57.483
current study profile blocks critical
findings retains high and lower

00:04:57.493 --> 00:05:01.538
findings as deferred risk and rejects
missing skipped malformed or

00:05:01.548 --> 00:05:05.784
inconsistent execution evidence The
retained local dashboard contains

00:05:05.794 --> 00:05:08.781
two hundred and fifty one observations
representing one hundred and

00:05:08.791 --> 00:05:12.667
eighty underlying issues The hosted
publication contains two hundred

00:05:12.677 --> 00:05:16.703
and fifty seven cross stage observations
Those datasets come from

00:05:16.713 --> 00:05:20.219
different runs and counting scopes so their
totals must remain separate

00:05:20.908 --> 00:05:24.295
Historical approvals also retain their
original expiry dates

00:05:27.194 --> 00:05:30.711
The hardened runtime uses a dedicated non
root identity with user

00:05:30.721 --> 00:05:34.077
and group identifier sixty five thousand
five hundred and thirty two

00:05:34.756 --> 00:05:38.892
It drops capabilities prevents privilege
escalation uses the runtime

00:05:38.902 --> 00:05:43.318
default seccomp profile and makes the root
filesystem read only The

00:05:43.328 --> 00:05:46.854
application still needs writable locations
for its database and selected

00:05:46.864 --> 00:05:51.250
training features Explicit mounts provide
those locations while protecting

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:53.557
application code and immutable seed content

00:05:55.458 --> 00:05:58.755
Historical infrastructure checks improved
from fifteen Kubernetes

00:05:58.765 --> 00:06:02.531
failures to one and Dockerfile failures
improved from two to zero

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:06.877
Those configuration improvements preceded
the later dependency repair

00:06:06.986 --> 00:06:11.212
so they are reported separately Selected
controls map to the documented

00:06:11.222 --> 00:06:16.117
CIS guidance but a full benchmark
certification is not claimed Network

00:06:16.127 --> 00:06:19.743
policy enforcement remains unverified and
must be addressed before

00:06:19.753 --> 00:06:21.681
a stronger deployment assurance claim

00:06:24.605 --> 00:06:27.951
Later remediation addressed the eleven
critical identities recorded

00:06:27.961 --> 00:06:32.427
in the baseline The changes include
dependency upgrades and replacements

00:06:32.526 --> 00:06:36.792
together with repairs to affected
application behavior The tests now

00:06:36.802 --> 00:06:40.059
assert rejection of the relevant unsafe
behavior rather than preserving

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:44.254
exploit success Retained source and rebuilt
image scans report zero

00:06:44.264 --> 00:06:45.243
critical findings

00:06:47.115 --> 00:06:50.561
The local image still has five high
observations so the result does

00:06:50.571 --> 00:06:54.927
not establish that the application is free
of vulnerabilities Syft

00:06:54.937 --> 00:06:58.373
produced a schema validated Cyclone DX
inventory with two thousand

00:06:58.383 --> 00:07:01.380
six hundred and fifty eight components for
the recorded local image

00:07:02.079 --> 00:07:05.196
The submission includes that existing
hardened image as an archive

00:07:05.206 --> 00:07:09.172
and a derived inventory that omits private
path metadata Provenance

00:07:09.182 --> 00:07:13.068
links both to their original receipt Local
image identity and the

00:07:13.078 --> 00:07:16.494
separate hosted image identity remain
explicitly distinguished

00:07:19.402 --> 00:07:22.908
The runtime evidence establishes that the
selected application behavior

00:07:22.918 --> 00:07:26.824
survives the hardening and critical repairs
Seven functional checks

00:07:26.834 --> 00:07:30.071
pass against the owned deployment and the
deployed image agrees with

00:07:30.081 --> 00:07:33.877
the relevant build receipt The passive ZAP
run reaches one hundred

00:07:33.887 --> 00:07:37.343
and twenty one URLs and verifies seed
routes including the home page

00:07:37.453 --> 00:07:42.488
product search languages FTP and metrics
Cleanup evidence confirms

00:07:42.498 --> 00:07:44.895
that the scanner and temporary resources
were removed

00:07:46.803 --> 00:07:51.328
The scan uses a traditional unauthenticated
crawler It does not establish

00:07:51.338 --> 00:07:55.084
full single page application navigation
role coverage business logic

00:07:55.094 --> 00:07:59.509
correctness or the results of active
attacks Some intentionally vulnerable

00:07:59.519 --> 00:08:02.826
training behavior remains visible including
directory listing and

00:08:02.836 --> 00:08:06.712
error disclosure Those observations stay in
the deferred register

00:08:07.411 --> 00:08:10.888
A successful runtime check proves a
specific expectation and does

00:08:10.898 --> 00:08:12.696
not establish complete security

00:08:15.613 --> 00:08:18.900
The dashboard measures detection on twenty
one deliberately selected

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:23.225
unsafe and repaired fixture cases Fifteen
cases contain introduced

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:28.290
issues The scanners catch fourteen and miss
one Six negative cases

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.786
are classified correctly and this small set
has no recorded false

00:08:31.796 --> 00:08:36.062
positives Precision is therefore one
hundred percent recall is ninety

00:08:36.072 --> 00:08:39.389
three point three percent and the F one
score is ninety six point

00:08:39.399 --> 00:08:40.118
six percent

00:08:41.983 --> 00:08:45.270
The known miss is an unprotected synthetic
export route that the six

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:49.585
authored source patterns do not detect
Retaining that miss helps explain

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:53.401
the rules coverage boundary The labels were
curated after the study

00:08:53.411 --> 00:08:57.807
work and have not received independent
validation These values describe

00:08:57.817 --> 00:09:02.252
scanner fixtures not AI accuracy and they
do not estimate recall across

00:09:02.262 --> 00:09:06.468
all remaining application vulnerabilities
The scenario target is met

00:09:06.478 --> 00:09:08.336
only within this limited fixture set

00:09:11.249 --> 00:09:14.456
The dashboard separates observations from
deduplicated underlying

00:09:14.466 --> 00:09:20.020
issues and exports the same data in HTML
JSON and CSV formats The

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:23.187
primary local snapshot contains one hundred
and eighty underlying

00:09:23.197 --> 00:09:26.953
issues including ninety one high severity
issues and zero critical

00:09:26.963 --> 00:09:31.119
issues Timing is useful only when the build
and setup scope is clear

00:09:31.818 --> 00:09:34.625
The repaired fresh directory run took two
hundred and seventy four

00:09:34.635 --> 00:09:37.812
point seven one pipeline seconds without
build or test reuse

00:09:39.681 --> 00:09:42.818
Its first actionable receipt arrived at one
hundred and sixty nine

00:09:42.828 --> 00:09:47.553
seconds Bootstrap downloads and cluster
creation add time outside

00:09:47.563 --> 00:09:51.629
that measurement A different historical run
reused a verified build

00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:55.635
and recorded ninety three point one nine
seconds Those timings are

00:09:55.645 --> 00:09:59.661
not interchangeable Each is one observation
so the dashboard does

00:09:59.671 --> 00:10:03.567
not infer percentile latency a service
level commitment or a measured

00:10:03.577 --> 00:10:05.135
production delivery improvement

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:12.086
The AI boundary constructs a new payload
from an exact field allowlist

00:10:12.765 --> 00:10:16.102
It does not forward raw scanner JSON and
hope that masking removes

00:10:16.112 --> 00:10:20.597
every sensitive value Generated aliases
replace local identifiers

00:10:20.697 --> 00:10:24.174
and advisory versions must come from the
independently verified scanner

00:10:24.184 --> 00:10:29.408
catalog The final serialized body receives
additional checks Captured

00:10:29.418 --> 00:10:33.674
mock requests demonstrate that private
paths source text secret canaries

00:10:33.774 --> 00:10:35.981
and scanner matches do not reach transport

00:10:37.835 --> 00:10:42.570
Invalid input refuses before a request is
sent Output validation checks

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:46.945
identifiers issue clusters versions
operations and required coverage

00:10:47.635 --> 00:10:51.900
Invented advisories unsupported versions
malformed fixes and omissions

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:56.865
fail validation The model receives no shell
or file write tools These

00:10:56.875 --> 00:11:00.701
deterministic controls establish boundary
behavior on the tested cases

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:04.867
They cannot prove how an unavailable live
model would perform across

00:11:04.877 --> 00:11:06.725
a representative evaluation set

00:11:09.642 --> 00:11:13.418
The configured external AI triage path
remains an open evaluation

00:11:13.428 --> 00:11:17.874
item A read only model lookup succeeded but
all three bounded generation

00:11:17.884 --> 00:11:22.269
attempts returned HTTP four twenty nine The
records do not establish

00:11:22.279 --> 00:11:26.675
the underlying cause No successful live
model output or returned usage

00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:30.531
record is available The project retains the
failed attempts and the

00:11:30.541 --> 00:11:31.769
exhausted request cap

00:11:33.639 --> 00:11:36.606
A deterministic twenty finding mock batch
passes through the same

00:11:36.616 --> 00:11:41.071
input boundary and output validation path
This verifies the integration

00:11:41.081 --> 00:11:45.586
contract and refusal controls on the tested
cases It cannot establish

00:11:45.596 --> 00:11:50.631
live model quality Live precision recall
hallucination frequency and

00:11:50.641 --> 00:11:54.677
actual billed cost therefore remain
unavailable The coding assistant

00:11:54.687 --> 00:11:58.024
contribution to implementation and
reporting is disclosed separately

00:11:58.723 --> 00:12:02.369
The next evaluation step needs working
authorized model access and

00:12:02.379 --> 00:12:03.868
independently labeled cases

00:12:06.789 --> 00:12:10.315
The three remediation proposals modify the
legacy baseline deployment

00:12:10.325 --> 00:12:14.910
manifest independently The first disables
service account token mounting

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.016
because the application does not use the
Kubernetes API The second

00:12:19.026 --> 00:12:23.571
explicitly requires non root execution and
the expected identity The

00:12:23.581 --> 00:12:27.268
third adds a bounded HTTP liveness probe
while retaining startup and

00:12:27.278 --> 00:12:31.543
readiness checks For each proposal the
selected Checkov control fails

00:12:31.553 --> 00:12:33.531
before the change and passes afterward

00:12:35.412 --> 00:12:38.859
The deployment checks also reach readiness
and pass selected HTTP

00:12:38.869 --> 00:12:43.284
expectations with cleanup recorded The
coding assistant authored bounded

00:12:43.294 --> 00:12:47.860
local templates The unavailable application
API did not generate them

00:12:48.569 --> 00:12:52.705
All three pull requests have now merged
into the feature branch Promotion

00:12:52.715 --> 00:12:55.801
then completed through develop and main
followed by the published

00:12:55.811 --> 00:12:59.947
version one point zero point zero release
Independent human review

00:12:59.957 --> 00:13:03.514
remains unverified so first review
correctness is still unmeasured

00:13:06.405 --> 00:13:09.641
Reproduction starts from a separate full
history checkout and uses

00:13:09.651 --> 00:13:13.607
project local pinned tools The script
rebuilds the application and

00:13:13.617 --> 00:13:17.204
image executes the scanner stages deploys
an owned temporary kind

00:13:17.214 --> 00:13:21.729
cluster runs passive DAST checks mock
triage and regenerates the dashboard

00:13:22.418 --> 00:13:26.624
Cleanup verifies removal of that run’s
cluster The submission preserves

00:13:26.634 --> 00:13:29.821
source history so that history scanning can
execute without relying

00:13:29.831 --> 00:13:31.129
on an unavailable remote

00:13:33.015 --> 00:13:36.421
Earlier fresh directory checks used the
same Docker host and standard

00:13:36.431 --> 00:13:40.487
caches They are not fresh machine tests and
the submission does not

00:13:40.497 --> 00:13:44.593
claim a new full pipeline execution today
The maturity assessment

00:13:44.603 --> 00:13:49.228
uses selected OWASP SAMM practices as an
organizing lens Repeatable

00:13:49.238 --> 00:13:54.243
builds security checks and defect records
demonstrate progress Independent

00:13:54.253 --> 00:13:57.879
review stronger deployment controls and
organizational evidence would

00:13:57.889 --> 00:13:59.987
be needed for a formal maturity assessment

00:14:02.904 --> 00:14:06.091
The submission brings together the three
required components this

00:14:06.101 --> 00:14:09.357
fifteen minute project presentation the
editable deck and technical

00:14:09.367 --> 00:14:13.893
report and the source code with related
project files The source snapshot

00:14:13.903 --> 00:14:17.279
now matches the published version one point
zero point zero release

00:14:17.968 --> 00:14:21.884
The package also includes full committed
history policy rules a prompt

00:14:21.894 --> 00:14:26.480
library the metrics dashboard and
verification receipts The recorded

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:30.116
local container and its inventory retain
their own exact image provenance

00:14:31.983 --> 00:14:35.410
The demonstrated engineering results are
six stage security coverage

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:39.096
identity checked evidence zero critical
findings in the retained repaired

00:14:39.106 --> 00:14:43.941
scans and tested controls around AI input
and output The remaining

00:14:43.951 --> 00:14:47.677
assessment work is successful live model
evaluation independent validation

00:14:47.687 --> 00:14:51.703
of labels and reviews and the student oral
assessment The package

00:14:51.713 --> 00:14:55.419
makes those boundaries visible for the
reviewer Thank you for reviewing

00:14:55.429 --> 00:14:57.737
Pipeline Fortress and the work of our
project team
